# Wold2025_UNCOVER_F410M_z7p2
# Paper: Wold et al. 2025, ApJ 980, 200, doi:10.3847/1538-4357/ada8a6; arXiv:2407.19023 (v1, the only arXiv version)
# Source: NO TABLE in the paper (arXiv v1 or published version). Values were extracted exactly from the vector
#   data of the arXiv v1 LF figure (source file lf_fancy.pdf; Fig. 13 of the published paper), black filled points
#   "This paper" (completeness-corrected);
#   the "uncorrected" (f=1) points are not used. Checked against published Fig. 13: same points.
#   logL values are the plotted bin positions (regular grid, spacing 0.2533 dex), hence the non-round numbers.
#   The text quotes 0.4 dex luminosity bins; bin edges are not given.
# Redshift: photometric F410M-excess selection, 6.72 < z < 7.59 (F410M half-power range); all luminosities are
#   computed at the assumed z = 7.17 (F410M pivot), hence file labelled z = 7.2 ("z~7" in the paper).
# Line: [O III] lambda5008, derived from the F410M excess with a fixed line template ([OIII]5008/Hbeta = 6.72;
#   the paper takes 5008 as ~64% of Hbeta+[OIII]); photometric candidates (2 NIRSpec-confirmed at the time).
# Field: UNCOVER (Abell 2744 lensing field), 13.68 arcmin^2 with deep HST veto; lensing-corrected luminosities and Veff
# Cosmology: H0 = 70, Om = 0.3
# Note: errors are 1-sigma Poisson only; only candidates with completeness > 5% used (31 sources).
#
# Columns:
# Log10(L_[OIII]5008 / erg s^-1)
# Log10(Phi / cMpc^-3 dex^-1)
# Lower 1-sigma delta in dex
# Upper 1-sigma delta in dex
#
41.214  -1.821  0.219  0.203
41.467  -2.157  0.200  0.187
41.720  -2.101  0.139  0.134
41.974  -2.802  0.341  0.295
42.227  -2.983  0.451  0.369
